course: dictionary
lesson: 11425
title: Acquired: got, learned, or gained over time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Acquire is a formal word for get or gain. Acquired is its past form, so it tells you something was got or learned in the past. «Sam acquired twelve new stickers at the fair.» Sam got twelve stickers, so acquired means got.
explain: Acquired can also mean learned. «Mia acquired the skill of riding a bike last summer.» Mia did not get the skill in a shop. She learned it through practice. Ask yourself: did someone get it, or learn it? The words around it are your clues.
explain: Acquired is also an adjective. «An acquired taste» is something you grow to like, like olives or dark chocolate, rather than liking it straight away. In science, acquired features are learned or caused by life, not inherited from parents.
fact: Acquired is the past form of acquire: acquire, acquires, acquired, acquiring.
fact: «Acquired» can mean got or gained by buying, being given, or working for something.
fact: «Acquired» can mean learned a skill, habit or knowledge.
fact: «An acquired taste» means something you learn to like over time.
fact: In science, acquired features are learned or caused by life, not inherited.
exercise: «Sam acquired twelve new stickers at the fair.» What does acquired mean here? | *Got | Counted | Lost | Gave away
exercise: «Ravi acquired a taste for olives after many dinners.» What does acquired a taste mean? | Forgot them | Bought a new plate | *Slowly learned to like them | Hated them at once
exercise: Which word is the past form of acquire? | acquiring | *acquired | acquires | acquire
test: «Zara acquired the skill of juggling after months of practice.» What does acquired mean here? | Broke | Born with | *Learned | Lost
test: In science, which is an acquired feature? | Blood group | Height from birth | Eye colour | *Knowing how to skateboard
exam: What does acquired mean in «The school acquired new computers this term»? | *Got | Broke | Lost | Sold
